fail[3]: With one kind allowed, the longest run is "aa", "bb" or "cc": 2.
fail[5]: With 0 kinds allowed, no letter fits: 0.
fail[6]: [1, 2, 1, 2] has two different values: 4.
hint: Add 1 to the count of `s[right]`.
hint: While `len(counts) > k`: take 1 from the count of `s[left]`, delete it at 0, and move left on.
hint: Record `right - left + 1`.
right: Each item enters the dictionary once and leaves at most once: O(n). Checking every start would be O(n × k) or worse.
wrong: Grow the window and count its values. While there are more than k kinds, drop items from the left, deleting a value whose count reaches 0. Each window that's left is valid, so keep the longest.

